  "title": "The Coffee Shop at the End of the Dungeon",
  "subtitle": "\"I retired from adventuring at thirty-eight. I opened a coffee shop. The coffee shop was inside a dungeon.\"",
  "penName": "Fen Holloway",
  "genre": "litrpgSystem",
  "hook": "I was a Rank A Spellsword for fifteen years. At thirty-eight I had enough gold, enough scars, and a specific disinterest in being a hero. I bought a retired-adventurer's dungeon for 3,400 gold and opened a coffee shop at the exit. The system classified it under **Hospitality/Craft — Level 1.** My first customer was Brem, a goblin bandit whose boss had died. He came for the smell. He stayed for the muffins. By the sixth week, I had seven monster regulars, three retired adventurers, and a system notification asking if I would like to found a Guild.",
